{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Prior-art research complete (OSS/spec survey; full briefing archived in session files). Findings:\n\nCONFIRMED MECHANISM (not yet a code root-cause proof, but strong): the `-32001 Request timed out` is raised by the MCP CLIENT SDK, not rebar's server. TS SDK default request timeout = 60s (`DEFAULT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MSEC = 60_000`, `resetTimeoutOnProgress` defaults FALSE). Python SDK (rebar's `mcp>=1.28.1,<2`) uses a single `anyio.fail_after(timeout)` window with NO progress-based reset in v1.x OR v2. rebar's server side is `anyio.fail_after(None)` = no deadline, so it keeps running + signs the op-cert after the client disconnects → the unknown-state + duplicate-paid-run symptoms.\n\nWHY OPTION (c) keepalive/progress is NOT viable for a 15-20 min op:\n- Python SDK has no `resetTimeoutOnProgress` (v1.x or v2); progress notifications do not extend the client deadline.\n- Spec (2026-07-28) guidance is only \"MAY reset timeout on progress, SHOULD cap anyway\" — optional client behavior, not reliable.\n- SSE resumability (`Last-Event-ID`) was REMOVED in 2026-07-28: any SSE break (nginx proxy_read_timeout, keepalive_timeout, blue-green flip) forces a re-issue with a NEW request id, which without dedup launches a 2nd billable run.\n- Closing the SSE stream IS cancellation per spec; a well-behaved client closes on timeout.\n\nRECOMMENDED (Option b) async job+poll via the official `io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks` extension: initial tools/call returns a taskId in ms (inside any client timeout); client polls `tasks/get`; `Mcp-Name: {taskId}` header enables nginx sticky routing to the process holding job state — the spec's own answer to rebar's nginx topology. Only active OSS reference impl found: mattzcarey/durable-mcp-server (Cloudflare DO, single-maintainer).\n\nIN-FLIGHT DEDUP (addresses the cost-amplification directly, spec is silent so it's app-level): singleflight-style registry keyed on `(ticket_id, gate_type, basis_ref)`. A 2nd call for the same key while a job runs attaches to the existing run instead of launching a 2nd paid LLM pass. Pure in-process — no CI dependency (portable), no client-capability dependency, no wire-protocol change. This is separable from and shippable before the full tasks migration.\n\nBLOCKERS/CAVEATS for the full (b): (1) rebar is on mcp v1.x (2025-03-26 wire protocol); tasks extension is v2-era — implementable manually in v1.x via the `add_response_router` seam or via a v2 migration. (2) Client capability unverified — must confirm Claude/Cursor declare `io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks` or the server must return `-32021` + need a sync fallback. (3) Blue-green durability needs an externalized task store (SQLite/Redis); the dedup registry itself can stay in-process.\n\nProposed phasing: Phase 1 = singleflight dedup (kills duplicate paid runs + gives a deterministic in-progress signal; document `review-plan --status` as the true-state recovery read). Phase 2 = full async job+poll (fixes the transport timeout at root), gated on verifying client tasks-capability. Escalating the phasing + scope decision to the operator."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788135191396268489,"uuid":"6fa19400-c3da-45d9-bb31-863bdee7b518"}